KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ make_exception_ptr: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ nested exception rethrown: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
no body for callee
--
make_exception_ptr has the body [propagation]/12 specifies; libstdc++'s
creates the exception object with __cxa_allocate_exception, which has no
model.  ~nested_exception (and libc++'s nested_exception constructor and
rethrow_nested) are defined in the compiled library and have models.
